<header class="ws-head"><p class="ws-kicker">Worksheet &middot; Songs in History</p><h1 class="ws-title">Worksheet: Songs of the early modern world</h1><p class="ws-lede">A worksheet on 27 songs of the early modern world in Songs in History: when and where they were made, what they say and how they sound.</p><p class="ws-who" aria-hidden="true"><span>Name</span><span>Class</span><span>Date</span></p><p class="ws-tools"><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="0">Print the worksheet</button><button type="button" class="ws-print" data-key="1">Print with the answers</button><a href="/songs/?e=earlymodern">Open the songs &rarr;</a></p></header>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><p class="ws-how">Number the songs from 1 (the oldest) to 6 (the newest).</p><ul class="ws-order"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Lekha Dodi</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Greensleeves</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Old 100th</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Pastime with Good Company</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Wilhelmus</span></li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Chad Gadya</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><p class="ws-how">Write the number of the right place next to each song. Their pages will help.</p><div class="ws-match"><ol class="ws-ma" type="A"><li>Chad Gadya</li><li>Hanuman Chalisa</li><li>Huron Carol</li><li>Wilhelmus</li><li>Ríu Ríu Chíu</li><li>Now Thank We All Our God</li></ol><ol class="ws-mb"><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Provence, France; Prague, Czech Republic</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Eilenburg, Saxony, Germany</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Spain (printed in Venice)</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Sainte-Marie among the Hurons, Canada</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Low Countries, Netherlands</li><li><span class="ws-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>Varanasi, India</li></ol></div></section>
<section class="ws-task"><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><ol class="ws-qs"><li><p>Read the words of <b>Pastime with Good Company</b> on its page (in English if they are in another language). What is the song about, and who might have sung it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Read the words of <b>Chad Gadya</b> on its page (in English if they are in another language). What is the song about, and who might have sung it?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Choose one song and listen to its performance. Which instruments or voices do you hear, and how does the music fit the words?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li><li><p>Songs travel: find a song on these pages that was sung far from where it was made, or that gave its tune to another song. How did it travel?</p><span class="ws-lines" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></span></li></ol></section>
<p class="ws-src">From The Epoch Institute: the-epoch-institute.org/songs/?e=earlymodern. Free to print and copy for use in class.</p>
<details class="ws-key" id="answers"><summary>Answer key</summary><div class="ws-key-b"><p class="ws-key-t">Answer key: Worksheet: Songs of the early modern world</p><section><h2><span class="ws-n">1</span>Put the songs in order</h2><ol class="ws-key-list"><li>Pastime with Good Company <span>c. 1513</span></li><li>Chad Gadya <span>c. 1527</span></li><li>Lekha Dodi <span>c. 1550</span></li><li>Old 100th <span>1561</span></li><li>Wilhelmus <span>1570</span></li><li>Greensleeves <span>1580</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">2</span>Where was each song made?</h2><ol class="ws-key-list" type="A"><li>Chad Gadya <span>1: Provence, France; Prague, Czech Republic</span></li><li>Hanuman Chalisa <span>6: Varanasi, India</span></li><li>Huron Carol <span>4: Sainte-Marie among the Hurons, Canada</span></li><li>Wilhelmus <span>5: Low Countries, Netherlands</span></li><li>Ríu Ríu Chíu <span>3: Spain (printed in Venice)</span></li><li>Now Thank We All Our God <span>2: Eilenburg, Saxony, Germany</span></li></ol></section><section><h2><span class="ws-n">3</span>Think and discuss</h2><p class="ws-key-note">Open questions: answers will vary. Good answers quote the song pages.</p></section></div></details>
